---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';

const title = 'Tips & FAQ | USIVA';
const description = 'Plain-language answers about visa planning, evidence, official sources, employer questions, and when to seek individualized immigration advice.';
const canonical = 'https://usiva.org/tips-faq.html';
---

<SiteLayout
  {title}
  {description}
  activePath="/tips-faq.html"
  {canonical}
  topbarMessage="Questions first · verify current instructions with the responsible authority."
  topbarLink={{ label: 'Open official tools', href: '/official-tools.html' }}
>
  <article class="faq-page">
    <header class="faq-hero">
      <div class="shell-container faq-hero__inner">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">USIVA / tips and FAQ</p>
          <h1>Questions worth asking before you act.</h1>
          <p class="faq-hero__lede">Use these answers to frame a visa or immigration question, identify the source that owns the next answer, and recognize when an official or professional review adds context.</p>
          <nav class="faq-actions" aria-label="FAQ actions">
            <a class="button button--primary" href="#questions">Read the questions</a>
            <a class="button button--outline" href="/visa-categories.html">Browse visa categories</a>
          </nav>
        </div>
        <aside class="faq-brief" aria-label="The USIVA planning posture">
          <span>Ask · verify · hand off</span>
          <strong>A complete file prepares a government conversation.</strong>
          <p>Organization makes a conversation clearer. The responsible agency, school, sponsor, employer, consulate, or qualified counsel controls the answer.</p>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="section section--paper" id="questions" aria-labelledby="faq-heading">
      <div class="shell-container faq-layout">
        <header class="faq-intro">
          <p class="eyebrow">Common questions</p>
          <h2 id="faq-heading">Start with the answer, then open the source.</h2>
          <p>These responses describe a planning posture. Current legal advice, government decisions, and category or status availability come from the responsible authority.</p>
          <nav class="faq-jumps" aria-label="FAQ sections">
            <a href="#readiness">Records</a>
            <a href="#authorization">Authorization</a>
            <a href="#escalate">Escalation</a>
          </nav>
        </header>

        <div class="faq-list">
          <details open>
            <summary>What is a readiness file?</summary>
            <p id="readiness">A private working set of identity, academic, funding, travel, prior-visa, family, employment, or program records relevant to the decision in front of you. Mark what is known, missing, dated, and still awaiting verification.</p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>What does a complete file establish?</summary>
            <p>A well-organized file makes a handoff clearer. The responsible authority determines eligibility, admissibility, work authorization, visa issuance, and government approval from the full record.</p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>Who should answer a university or status question?</summary>
            <p>Start with the written instructions for the program and the designated school official or sponsor named for the situation. Questions about personal history, status, or legal interpretation may require qualified immigration counsel.</p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>Are study, research, training, travel, and employment the same activity?</summary>
            <p id="authorization">They involve different permissions, documents, and timing. Describe the actual activity, who directs it, whether compensation is involved, and whether written authorization is required before it begins.</p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>Can I begin work while I wait for an answer?</summary>
            <p>Confirm with the responsible school, sponsor, government source, employer, or attorney before beginning anything that may be training, research, or employment. A submitted form, invitation, or role interest becomes useful context for that review.</p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>What does USIVA provide?</summary>
            <p>USIVA provides visa and immigration planning, document organization, official-source navigation, and responsible handoff prompts. Legal representation, filings, eligibility, admission, employment, funding, visa issuance, work authorization, and government approval belong to the responsible authority or qualified counsel.</p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>Why do sources and dates matter?</summary>
            <p>Rules, fees, school instructions, sponsor requirements, and program details can change. A source serves its defined status, institution, location, and date; compare it with your facts. Save the source and the date you checked it.</p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>When does a question need an official or professional review?</summary>
            <p id="escalate">General content points to the responsible authority when the answer depends on a prior refusal, status concern, criminal or immigration history, a complex work arrangement, a change of status, or another personal fact. Prepare the facts and use that authority, including licensed counsel when appropriate.</p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>Should I send sensitive documents through this site?</summary>
            <p>Submit passwords, passport numbers, receipt numbers, identity documents, and private case records only through the verified channel requested by the responsible agency, school, employer, sponsor, or counsel.</p>
          </details>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section section--mist" aria-labelledby="next-heading">
      <div class="shell-container next-grid">
        <header>
          <p class="eyebrow">Continue with a source</p>
          <h2 id="next-heading">Take the smallest useful next step.</h2>
        </header>
        <ul class="next-list">
          <li><a href="/visa-categories.html"><strong>Visa category directory</strong><span>Start with purpose and follow the official route.</span></a></li>
          <li><a href="/official-tools.html"><strong>USCIS and State tools</strong><span>Go directly to case status, MyUSCIS, Visa Wizard, and the Visa Bulletin.</span></a></li>
          <li><a href="/employers.html"><strong>Employer resources</strong><span>Orient Form I-9, E-Verify, and company-side handoffs.</span></a></li>
          <li><a href="/briefs.html"><strong>Research briefs</strong><span>Read source-led explanations with visible limits.</span></a></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="faq-notice" aria-label="USIVA boundary">
      <div class="shell-container"><strong>USIVA boundary:</strong> informational planning and official-source navigation only. Current USCIS, State Department, DHS, school, sponsor, employer, consular, and qualified-counsel instructions control.</div>
    </section>
  </article>
</SiteLayout>

<style>
  .faq-hero {
    background: var(--color-navy-deep);
    color: var(--color-paper);
  }

  .faq-hero .eyebrow {
    color: var(--color-paper);
  }

  .faq-hero__inner {
    align-items: end;
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.1fr) minmax(18rem, 0.72fr);
    padding-block: clamp(2.75rem, 5vw, 5rem);
  }

  .faq-hero h1 {
    color: var(--color-paper);
    font-size: clamp(2.35rem, 4.35vw, 4.25rem);
    max-width: 13ch;
  }

  .faq-hero__lede {
    color: var(--color-on-dark-muted);
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    line-height: 1.5;
    margin-block-start: var(--space-2);
    max-width: 58ch;
  }

  .faq-actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-1);
    margin-block-start: var(--space-3);
  }

  .faq-brief {
    border-top: 0.3rem solid var(--color-highlight);
    background: var(--color-navy);
    padding: var(--space-3);
  }

  .faq-brief > span {
    color: var(--color-paper);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--step--2);
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .faq-brief strong {
    display: block;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--step-2);
    line-height: 1.05;
    margin-block: var(--space-2);
  }

  .faq-brief p {
    color: var(--color-on-dark-muted);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .faq-layout {
    display: grid;
    gap: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 5rem);
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.72fr) minmax(0, 1.28fr);
  }

  .faq-intro h2,
  .next-grid h2 {
    max-width: 18ch;
  }

  .faq-intro > p:last-of-type {
    margin-block-start: var(--space-2);
    max-width: 44ch;
  }

  .faq-jumps {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-line);
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.8rem 1.1rem;
    margin-block-start: var(--space-3);
    padding-block-start: var(--space-2);
  }

  .faq-jumps a {
    color: var(--color-accent-dark);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    font-weight: 750;
  }

  .faq-list {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-line-dark);
  }

  .faq-list details {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-line);
    padding-block: var(--space-2);
  }

  .faq-list summary {
    color: var(--color-navy-deep);
    cursor: pointer;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    font-weight: 700;
    list-style-position: outside;
    padding-inline: 0.3rem;
  }

  .faq-list p {
    max-width: 70ch;
    padding: var(--space-1) 1.5rem 0.2rem 0.3rem;
  }

  .next-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.7fr) minmax(0, 1.3fr);
  }

  .next-list {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-line);
    list-style: none;
  }

  .next-list li {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-line);
  }

  .next-list a {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.25rem;
    padding-block: var(--space-2);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .next-list strong {
    color: var(--color-navy-deep);
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--step-1);
  }

  .next-list span {
    color: var(--color-muted);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
  }

  .faq-notice {
    background: var(--color-navy);
    color: var(--color-on-dark-muted);
    padding-block: var(--space-2);
  }

  .faq-notice strong {
    color: var(--color-paper);
  }

  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .faq-hero__inner,
    .faq-layout,
    .next-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
